# PRO-241: nanopb-generated protobuf sources are BUILD ARTIFACTS, never committed.
# The codegen pre-step (nanopb's platformio_generator.py) emits them into
# $BUILD_DIR/nanopb/generated-src (under .pio/, already ignored above); this
# rule additionally guards against a stray *.pb.{c,h} landing in the source tree
# if the generator is ever run by hand. The .proto is the only committed source.
*.pb.c
*.pb.h
# ...except the spike's pinned design-record output (committed as the PRO-239 record).
!docs/spike-nanopb-comms/gen/*.pb.c
!docs/spike-nanopb-comms/gen/*.pb.h
bean-whisperer/
.worktrees/
.playwright-mcp
.superpowers/
playwright/
output/
.claude/settings.local.json
*.png
!docs/**/*.png
!ui/**/*.png
!icons/**/*.png
!web/public/**/*.png
!web/src/**/*.png
!assets/**/*.png

# Desktop simulator (CAR-399) runtime state and build artifacts
sim_data/
*.bmp

# Stray alternate build dir
.pio-car340/

# PRO-358: ESP-IDF/CMake build-model artifacts. Setting custom_sdkconfig (the
# NimBLE-PSRAM fix on [env:display]) makes the pioarduino platform build the
# project via the "Arduino as IDF component" model, which drops these generated
# files at the project root. They are build outputs (regenerated every build),
# never source — keep them out of git.
/sdkconfig.defaults
/sdkconfig.*
/CMakeLists.txt
/dependencies.lock
/managed_components/
/.dummy/
